  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1111 AM CDT Wed Sep 16 2026\n\nThe main points for the long term forecast will be daily \nprecipitation chances and a possible cool down next week. The upper \nridging is expected to gradually move back east beginning Friday \nbringing southwesterly flow aloft ushering in subtropical moisture \nto the mid-to-upper levels. Precipitation chances on Friday will \nprimarily remain along and just east of the NM/TX border as \nsubsidence from the upper ridging keeps the rest of the forecast \narea dry. Widespread precipitation chances are expected beginning \nSaturday as the upper ridging is expected to be well east of the \nforecast area. Multiple passing shortwaves will prolong \nprecipitation chances everyday through at least mid-week. Hot \ntemperatures expected Friday with highs in the 90s across the \nregion. Saturday will be the start of a cool down through next week \nwith widespread precipitation and clouds. Some areas by early to mid \nnext week could see highs in the lower 80s. However, if the upper \nridging does not shift east as some models are predicting, we most \nlikely will see dry conditions and hot temperatures.",
